      "writtenOn": "2022-02-08T14:15:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Given that buffer, texture proxy, and copy data already have some indirection and UploadCommand itself isn\u0027t that large of an object, is the main goal of switching std::unique_ptr or bool+ptr to handle errors?\n\nIf that\u0027s the case, what if we made it so that UploadCommand can\u0027t fail, and UploadList::appendUpload() handles the steps/work to get buffer and copy data prepared? If that fails, then it can return a bool and not modify its fCommands list. \n\nThis is coming mostly from wanting to avoid vectors of unique ptrs, and avoiding ref/unref indirection when possible. But if the plan is to make UploadCommand bigger and more complex, then my ideas don\u0027t apply as well.",
      "parentUuid": "6f582cd5_1c9b69f2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 39,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 39,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "a3e19b8c5359afeedb2550bf0dead88a4ead3491",
